eded.\n\n- **Dashboard** — active (new gallery UI + launch mechanics). Owner: RHOAI\n  Dashboard (per `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`).\n- **Notebooks** — passive: no notebook-controller or workbench code changes;\n  tutorials run in existing workbenches against pinned workbench images.\n  Validation becomes acceptance criteria on the tutorial content epic.\n- **Data Science Pipelines** — passive: no DSP code changes; the pipeline\n  tutorial imports through the existing DataSciencePipelinesApplication /\n  KFP v2 surfaces. Validation becomes acceptance criteria on the tutorial\n  content epic.\n- **Documentation** — active for content only (`docs-authoring`\n  implementation type). It has no architecture-context file, but it is a\n  content-process component, not a new platform component to provision — no\n  onboarding chain is generated (Rule 20 does not apply).\n\nComponent mapping notes (non-obvious mappings):\n- The tutorial packaging format epic is assigned to **Dashboard** because the\n  gallery's launch mechanics are the consuming surface that parses the format;\n  the Dashboard team owns the contract.\n- The curated tutorial content epic is assigned to **Notebooks** (owner:\n  Workbenches) as the single most-relevant canonical name — five of the six\n  tutorials are notebooks and all launch into workbenches — and spans Data\n  Science Pipelines for the \"first pipeline\" tutorial (noted here per the\n  single-most-relevant-name rule).\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format: metadata, pinned images, validation manifest | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 (inherited — gates all P0 work) |\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery and one-click launch | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Six curated tutorials covering the core journeys | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Tutorial gallery usage and contribution documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E002[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 Dashboard gallery and launch\"]\n    E001 --> E003[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 Curated tutorials\"]\n    E001 --> E004[\"RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 Documentation\"]\n    E002 --> E004\n    E003 --> E004\n```\n\nCritical path: E001 → E002 → E004 (and E001 → E003 → E004), length 3.\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (artifact another epic builds against) | The gallery's launch mechanics build against the packaging format — they parse tutorial metadata and use the pinned images. The format is a contract artifact, not a configuration reference. |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact another epic builds against) | Tutorials are packaged per the format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest); content cannot be authored or validated before the contract exists. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation must describe the packaging format that was actually defined. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation must describe the gallery that was actually built. |\n| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | The contribution-process documentation must reflect the real tutorial set and its validation. |\n| E002 ∥ E003 (no edge) | Rule 14 (different components/teams, no shared artifact) | The gallery is verified against any tutorial conforming to the format (a fixture); tutorials are validated via their validation manifests, not via the gallery. No shared artifact, so the two streams run in parallel. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Gallery surface + one-click launch into the user's project (workbench with notebook, or pipeline import). |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Six tutorials, each packaged and tested against the current release; passive-component validation for Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines lives here as acceptance criteria. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Priority-split analysis: not bundled with the gallery and not deferrable — the format is a distinct deliverable (a versioned contract) that both P0 epics build against, so by priority inheritance the epic is P0 (an epic blocking all P0 work is implicitly P0). The P1 label on HLR-3 reads as relative value, not a deferral signal; shipping the gallery or the tutorials first would mean building the same contract ad hoc inside those epics. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | `docs-authoring` priority exception: strategy frontmatter priority is Major → epic priority P1 (not P2, and no priority push upstream). |\n\nFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\nNon-blocking — human verification recommended:\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no NFRs;\n   Affected Components are listed without change descriptions or owners.\n   Owner teams were derived from architecture context (Dashboard → RHOAI\n   Dashboard, Notebooks → Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI\n   Pipelines) and epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs.\n2. **Team assumptions.** The tutorial content epic is assigned to Workbenches\n   (most-relevant canonical component: Notebooks) because the strategy names\n   no content owner; the documentation epic is assigned to an assumed\n   \"RHOAI Documentation\" team. Both should be confirmed by the strat owner.\n3. **Passive-component risk.** Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines are\n   passive (no code changes; tutorials exercise existing GA surfaces). If\n   tutorial validation exposes gaps in either component on the current\n   release, component work outside this decomposition would be needed.\n4. **Scope trap watch.** Out-of-scope explicitly excludes community\n   contribution intake tooling and localization. HLR-4's contribution-process\n   documentation must describe the process without promising submission\n   tooling — this is stated as an acceptance criterion on the documentation\n   epic.\n5. **Epic size / re-split triggers.** The gallery epic (one feature surface:\n   browse + two launch mechanics) and the tutorial epic (one curated,\n   co-validated set of six) may each exceed a sprint of effort. They are kept\n   as single logical changes because a split would duplicate the\n   format-conformance and validation pass across fragments. Re-split triggers:\n   - E002: re-split if the workbench-launch and pipeline-import mechanics\n     together exceed a sprint — split along the two launch surfaces.\n   - E003: split by journey cluster (notebook tutorials vs the pipeline\n     tutorial, which involves the Data Science Pipelines team) if authoring\n     and validation exceed a sprint of effort.\n\nNo priority inversions were found: E001's P0 is inheritance-driven (it gates\nall P0 work), and E004's P1 is the docs-authoring exception (Major → P1).\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\ntiming; all work is internal to the platform.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34917,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-903b1fe713702bfa","agent_id":"aba7fb9fdd72707ee","session_id":"a9cf95da-4842-4821-bfce-05c3c9153e25","uuid":"547d9e7b-cc43-4453-8c8c-4007c1ddbad4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:06:33.848Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
