{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b591bd6f12e675c0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tNot below-threshold and not docs-only. The strategy explicitly spans three\n15\tarchitecturally distinct work streams with different owners and review\n16\tprocesses — product code (the gallery and launch mechanics), substantive\n17\tcontent authoring (the tutorials themselves), and documentation — across four\n18\taffected components (Dashboard, Notebooks, Data Science Pipelines,\n19\tDocumentation). The multiple-distinct-work-streams escape condition applies,\n20\tso the strategy receives a full multi-epic decomposition.\n21\t\n22\t## Step 1 — Strategy Structure\n23\t\n24\t- **High Level Requirements**: HLR-1 (P0, gallery + one-click launch),\n25\t  HLR-2 (P0, six curated tested tutorials), HLR-3 (P1, tutorial packaging\n26\t  format), HLR-4 (P2, gallery + contribution documentation).\n27\t- **Affected Components**: Dashboard, Notebooks, Data Science Pipelines,\n28\t  Documentation (listed as bullets — no change descriptions or owner teams).\n29\t- **Open Questions**: none. No conditional ADRs, pending reviews, or risks\n30\t  table → no Investigation epics.\n31\t- **Staff Engineer Input**: not present in the strategy — no overrides.\n32\t- Missing sections (health warnings, see below): Impacted Teams table,\n33\t  Dependencies table, Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, Non-Functional\n34\t  Requirements. Owner teams were derived from architecture context; epic\n35\t  acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs.\n36\t\n37\t## Step 2 — Component Graph\n38\t\n39\tAll four affected components are canonical RHAI Jira component